      <activity id="08541871-b8ed-50ce-9041-7ea56c68ce96" activityNameId="011a9eb1-9a8d-5847-80f9-8a1f466ce985" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Refrigerant R134a, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Refrigerant R134a, at plant
It has been assumed that 50% of R134a is produced from trichlorethylene and 50% from tetrachloroethylene. Data based on (Frischknecht 1999);
Formula: C2H2F4; 
Synonyms: working fluid, cooling fluid, HFC-134a, 1,1,1,2-Tetrafluorethan, 1,1,1,2-tetrafluoroethane; 
UUID: ddce4dc4-2356-3d77-8208-187e6598018d
The module includes chemicals, energy and transport requirements for R134a production. 
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: none
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_ddce4dc4-2356-3d77-8208-187e6598018d.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
